On NAO, I usually let the RNG pick a character for me. My current one is
a (human) healer. I decided to use the protection racket. Since I play
carefully, even if I'm not playing the protection racket, this usually
doesn't give me much problems.

I did hit some monsters accidentally, but a single shop in the main
dungeon got me to over 5000 zorkmids, at which point I decided to try
the Mines. Me and my pet got down to level 5, when Rothond stepped into
a trap door before my very eyes. I had was halfway clearing that (dark)
level, and my wand of light had run out. I took the gamble and jumped
after Rothond, hoping to land on the same level as he might have ended
up upon.

I didn't. I landed on Mines level 10, at EXP 1/16. I did have two wands
of sleep left, a wand of magic missile, and a wand of striking. Level 10
proved to be a bones level, with a wizard that had been petrified by
some chickatrices.

I decided to stop the protection racket, and go for a single donation
(staying below level 12 should be possible, if I could keep that
character alive in the first place :-) ).

I managed to get back to level 6 after a long and arduous trek through
the dungeon, being level 7 myself when I got there. I had enough money
for a single donation, which yielded only two points of AC, the
guaranteed minimum...

On my way back, I found Rothond, who was still tame! Not long after
that, I foolishly put on an unidentified helmet from that bones level,
which, of course, was a helmet of opposite alignment. Bye, bye, two
points of AC which I'd fought so fiercely for to obtain.  :-)

Well, it won't take much time or I'll have enough to buy me a next
point, I'm now level 8 with about 3100 gold left... And a nymph has rid
me of that cursed helmet.

Did I mention that that bones level also had the cursed Magicbane, a
cursed +1 cloak of magic resistance, and an as yet unopened bag of
holding?

